CORE PHILOSOPHY:

**REWARD these approaches:**
- ✓ Loosening strict sequences into partial_order when both orders appear
- ✓ Large maximal partial_order blocks (many activities in parallel)
- ✓ Generalizing repeated behavior into simple/single activity loops
- ✓ Using optional() instead of duplicating branches
- ✓ Simple universal structures over complex trace-fitting
- ✓ High fitness on dominant traces (≥ 95% of log)
- ✓ Reasonable precision — model does not allow wildly unrealistic behavior

**PENALIZE these approaches:**
- ✗ Over-sequencing (forcing A→B when B→A also occurs)
- ✗ Small fragmented partial_order blocks (should be merged)
- ✗ Activity duplication across branches
- ✗ Complex nested structures when simple parallel blocks work
- ✗ Overfitting to rare traces (< 5%) at the cost of simplicity
- ✗ Low fitness on dominant traces (model blocks behavior seen in > 20% of cases)
- ✗ Extremely low precision (model allows behavior completely unseen in log)

