SCORING PHILOSOPHY:

**Score = Base (correctness) + Generalization Bonus + Fitness/Precision Bonus - Complexity Penalty**

START WITH:
- 0.5 if structurally valid and covers main activities
- Then adjust up or down

ADJUST UPWARD (+0.1 to +0.2):
- ✓ Uses large maximal partial_order blocks appropriately
- ✓ Avoids over-sequencing
- ✓ Clean, simple structure
- ✓ Good generalization of dominant behavior
- ✓ Minimal, well-scoped loops

ADJUST UPWARD (fitness/precision bonus):
- +0.10 if model clearly replays ≥ 95% of dominant traces
- +0.05 if precision is reasonable (no wildly unseen behavior allowed)

ADJUST DOWNWARD:
- -0.3 to -0.5: Structural errors, invalid POWL
- -0.2 to -0.3: Activity duplication, major rule violations
- -0.10 to -0.20: Over-sequencing when should parallelize, fragmented partial_orders
- -0.10: Fitness on dominant traces clearly low (blocks > 50% of cases)
- -0.05 to -0.10: Minor unnecessary complexity
- -0.05: Precision very low (allows completely unseen behavior)
- -0.01 to -0.05: Missing rare patterns < 5% (barely matters)

**DO NOT PENALIZE:**
- Model allows more behavior than log shows due to parallelization
- Loose ordering constraints (this is GOOD generalization)
- Blocks rare/noisy traces under 5% (this is GOOD precision)
- Precision loss caused by intentional large partial_order blocks

**FINAL SCORE RANGES:**
- **0.9-1.0**: Excellent - Simple, universal, valid, high fitness on dominant traces
- **0.8-0.9**: Good - Minor complexity or small fitness gaps
- **0.6-0.7**: Acceptable - Some over-sequencing or moderate fitness issues
- **0.4-0.5**: Poor - Too complex, over-strict, or low fitness
- **0.0-0.3**: Failed - Invalid or fundamentally wrong

